You hit the nail on the head! Looking at your React code, I can see the exact **Race Condition** causing this "stale state" bug.
### The Root Cause: The Race Condition
When you click "Start Validation" for your *second* file, here is the exact sequence of events happening in your code:
 1. You click "Start Validation".
 2. handleStartValidation immediately sets setIsProcessing(true).
 3. Your useEffect is watching for changes. It sees isProcessing is now true, and it looks at your requestId state.
 4. **THE BUG:** Because you didn't clear the requestId from the *first* upload, the requestId state is still holding the ID of the 1,06,720 row file!
 5. The useEffect instantly fires a status check for the **old** file before your new file even finishes uploading.
 6. The backend replies "SUCCESS! That old file has 1,06,720 rows!"
 7. The useEffect sets isProcessing(false), updates the rows, and pushes you to the next screen. A split second later, your new file finishes uploading, but the UI has already moved on.
### The Fix
You just need to clear the requestId and totalRows the moment a new file is selected or validation starts.
Here are the two exact places you need to update in your frontend file:
#### 1. Update validateAndSetFile
Find the validateAndSetFile function and add setRequestId(null) and setTotalRows(0) when a new file is successfully accepted.
**Change this:**
```javascript
    setFile(selected);
    setIsCsvFile(fileName.endsWith(".csv"));
    setResultStatus(null);
    setResultMsg("");
    setValidationStage(0);
    setPreviewRows([]);
    setAutoDlTriggered(false);
    setIsProcessing(false);
    setDownloadMsg("Downloading error report...");
  };

```
**To this:**
```javascript
    setFile(selected);
    setIsCsvFile(fileName.endsWith(".csv"));
    setResultStatus(null);
    setResultMsg("");
    setValidationStage(0);
    setPreviewRows([]);
    setTotalRows(0);        // FIX: Clear the old row count
    setRequestId(null);     // FIX: Clear the old request ID
    setAutoDlTriggered(false);
    setIsProcessing(false);
    setDownloadMsg("Downloading error report...");
  };

```
#### 2. Update handleStartValidation
To be absolutely safe, also clear the requestId right before you set isProcessing to true.
**Change this:**
```javascript
    triggerDebounce();
    setResultStatus(null);
    setResultMsg("");
    setValidationStage(0);
    setIsProcessing(true);
    setAutoDlTriggered(false);
    setDownloadMsg("Downloading error report...");

```
**To this:**
```javascript
    triggerDebounce();
    setResultStatus(null);
    setResultMsg("");
    setValidationStage(0);
    setRequestId(null);     // FIX: Prevent the useEffect from polling the old ID
    setIsProcessing(true);
    setAutoDlTriggered(false);
    setDownloadMsg("Downloading error report...");

```
### Why this works:
By setting setRequestId(null), when setIsProcessing(true) happens, the useEffect will say "Oh, isProcessing is true, but there is no requestId yet. I will wait."
It will wait patiently until the callApi finishes uploading the new file and calls setRequestId(data.requestId). Then the useEffect will wake up and poll the correct file, showing you your 75,000 rows!
